# Explain Abstraction
Abstraction is the process of breaking down complex ideas ,concepts into simple ones by focusing on essential, genal features while removing unnecessary characteristics so that only the essential ones remain.
THe key benefits include reduced complexity.
An application of abstractions is Programming with classes.
Example of abstrAactions :
 public class Person
    {
        public string _givenName = "";
        public string _familyName = "";

        public Person()
        {
        }

        public void ShowEasternName()
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"{_familyName}, {_givenName}");
        }

        public void ShowWesternName()
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"{_givenName} {_familyName}");
        }
    }

